<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 11.5 trln rbls of bills, bonds.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 11.5 trln rbls of bills, bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will offer 7.50 trillion roubles of 182-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22083) and four trillion roubles in an additional 714-day tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bond (series 24012) on May 14, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		22083</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		   May 14, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			  182 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		Nov 12, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		24012</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		   May 14, 1997</p>
<p>    Initial issue date	 April 30, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	  714 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		April 28, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date	  Oct 29, 1997</p>
<p>    Coupon rate		  32.52 pct</p>
<p>In money terms the coupon rate is 162,155 roubles less accruals of 12,473.46 roubles.</p>
<p>On May 14 the Finance Ministry will also repay about 7.18 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 224-day T-bills (series 23052).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
